# PROTECT_ZENJXL failures: 0 cells
# Libjxl differs from Zenjxl: 27/27 cells
#
# Per cell:
#   - zenjxl_bytes / libjxl_bytes: bitstream size
#   - libjxl_minus_zenjxl_bytes: positive = Libjxl strategy bigger
#   - cjxl_bytes: libjxl reference encode (cjxl v0.12.0)
#   - *_ssim2: fast-ssim2 on sRGB u8 (higher is better, 0..100)
#   - *_bfly: in-process Rust butteraugli on linear RGB (lower is better)
#
# DO NOT (future agents):
# - DO NOT flip cfl_newton_libjxl_parity = true at the default path.
#   The W44-183 measurement (286bf5f1) demonstrated 25/27 photo cells
#   regress SSIM2 by 0.25-13.02 + 7.82% mean bytes when this fires
#   in isolation. The downstream cost-model calibration (W44-29..W44-172)
#   is tuned for the effective-LS-warm-start baseline.
# - DO NOT promote this to LeanFaster. LeanFaster keeps the same
#   cost-model calibration as Zenjxl; the W44-183 regression would
#   fire identically.
# - DO NOT remove the JXL_W44_184_FORCE_LIBJXL_NEWTON env hook.
